! Rocksalt LiF -- the cell of Elk's examples/TDDFT-optics/LiF-bootstrap, which
! is the canonical demonstration of the bootstrap TDDFT kernel (Sharma,
! Dewhurst, Sanna and Gross, PRL 107, 186401 (2011)). LiF has a strongly bound
! exciton: a sharp peak below the gap that RPA does not produce at all.
!
! avec there is 3.80402 bohr on the fcc primitive vectors, so alat = 7.60804.
! LDA (pz) to match Elk's xctype = 3; norm-conserving HGH, the only LDA
! norm-conserving Li and F in the Quantum ESPRESSO library. Li has no semicore,
! so this has 4 occupied bands where Elk's all-electron run has 6 -- the two
! extra are the 1s cores, which no optical transition here touches.
!
! The k-grid below is what an SCF needs. A *spectrum* needs the whole grid
! rather than a wedge, which is what run_absorption's `kpoints` argument is for.
! Elk's reference output is committed beside this file as
! reference.out.elk-lif-bootstrap.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 7.60804, nat = 2, ntyp = 2,
    ecutwfc = 80.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
    mixing_beta = 0.7
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Li  6.941   Li.pz-hgh.UPF
 F   18.998  F.pz-hgh.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 Li 0.00 0.00 0.00
 F  0.50 0.50 0.50
K_POINTS (automatic)
 8 8 8 0 0 0
